From 5e8d8510ee10bae9842b6678d6edb563931797b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:15:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298: host-path kv-zero drain holds the queue lock
 through unique_lock (exception safe)

f2ac86ff9a locked the compute queue handle with lock()/unlock() around
vkQueueWaitIdle; a throw from waitIdle (device lost) would leak the queue
mutex. vk_queue_handle is BasicLockable (virtual lock/unlock), so a scoped
std::unique_lock does the same work and releases on unwind. No behaviour
change on the normal path.

Origin: lane-298
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED (same gate as f2ac86ff9a: kvzo cell, ids vs v0.1.3.1 + served ABBA)
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
index b369d77cfd..0877f20001 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
@@ -1700,10 +1700,11 @@ void ggml_vk_buffer_memset(vk_buffer& dst, size_t offset, uint32_t c, size_t siz
         // lane-298 (HQ86 18:42): same race as the GPU path; drain the compute queue so no in-flight graph write lands
         // after the CPU zero. waitIdle, not a fence submit: a pool cleanup here would reset an open batch's buffer.
         std::lock_guard<std::recursive_mutex> guard(dst->device->mutex);
-        vk_queue_handle & q = *dst->device->compute_queue->handle;
-        q.lock();
-        q.queue.waitIdle();
-        q.unlock();
+        {
+            vk_queue_handle & q = *dst->device->compute_queue->handle;
+            std::unique_lock<vk_queue_handle> ql(q);
+            q.queue.waitIdle();
+        }
         memset((uint8_t*)dst->ptr + offset, c, size);
         return;
     }
